      <h1>The Brazos Region</h1>
      <p>
        The country along the Brazos River — some of the oldest farmed and
        ranched land in Texas. Honest Acres Group advertises in this region
        on Land.com and LandWatch, where James serves as a buyer's agent
        representative: if you're shopping Brazos country, he's the agent
        who'll walk it with you and tell you the truth about it.
      </p>

      <h2>The land</h2>
      <p>
        Rich river-bottom soils and native pecan bottoms along the Brazos
        and its tributaries, rolling improved pasture above the bottoms, and
        serious surface water — river frontage, creeks, stock tanks, and
        lake country within an easy drive. It's ground that can run cattle,
        cut hay, grow crops, and hunt, sometimes all on the same tract.
      </p>

      <h2>Why buyers come here</h2>
      <p>
        <strong>Production:</strong> fertile bottoms and improved pasture — real cattle, hay, and farm country.<br />
        <strong>Water:</strong> the river itself, plus lake access across the region.<br />
        <strong>Wildlife:</strong> whitetail and dove in the bottoms, hogs year-round, waterfowl on the tanks.<br />
        <strong>Access:</strong> centered on Bryan–College Station and Brenham — real country, well west of the Metroplex sprawl and an easy run from Houston, without giving up town when you need it.
      </p>

      <h2>Counties we work here</h2>
      <p>The Brazos Region as LandWatch defines it — seven counties: Washington, Grimes, Brazos, Burleson, Leon, Robertson, and Madison. Talk to James about the tract you're eyeing, wherever it sits in the region.</p>

